# build/container/Dockerfile build context trim. Keep this conservative:
# only exclude directories the boid binary's `go build .` (and its go:embed
# directives under web/, internal/skills, internal/db/migrate,
# internal/initwizard) never touch. See build/container/Dockerfile's header
# comment for what the image build actually needs.
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.codex/
docs/
e2e/
*.md
LICENSE

# The metaproject library's own unit tests. They are part of the boid repo (CI
# runs them) but have no business inside a job's skills directory: an agent
# browsing ~/.claude/skills/boid-metaproject/ should see the scripts it can run
# and the docs it should read, not a test suite it will mistake for either.
#
# go:embed happens to skip them too (a leading "_" is excluded unless the
# pattern says all:), but the two exclusions are NOT the same rule and do not
# produce the same tree: that same underscore rule also drops
# scripts/boidmeta/__init__.py from the embedded copy, which this COPY keeps.
# Harmless — DeployAll has no production caller (the image path is what jobs
# see) and boidmeta still imports as a namespace package — but do not read
# either exclusion as a statement about the other.
internal/skills/data/boid-metaproject/scripts/_tests/

# Python bytecode from running those tests locally. Without this, a developer
# who ran the suite before `docker build` ships .pyc files into
# /opt/boid/skills — stale ones, since the image's python is 3.11 and the
# host's may not be.
**/__pycache__/
